@startuml
actor Developer
participant "Workload API" as API
participant "Shared planner" as Planner
participant "Definition matcher / dependency graph" as Graph
participant "Immutable template source" as Source
participant "Template Driver worker" as Renderer
participant "Existing Terraform lifecycle" as Terraform
participant "CD / Fleet" as CD
database "Revision / delivery artifacts" as Revision
Developer -> API: Save Generic Workload
API -> API: Normalize / validate / CAS draft
Developer -> API: Preview
API -> Planner: Consistent snapshot
Planner -> Graph: Match workload Definition / resolve references
Graph --> Planner: Definition revision, graph, target, bindings
Planner -> Source: Read verified immutable content/inputs
Planner -> Renderer: Symbolic preview (no provider calls)
Renderer --> API: Validated safe manifest review / token
Developer -> API: Deploy(token)
API -> Planner: Verify pinned snapshots
API -> Terraform: Existing provider-first batches
Terraform --> API: Resolved outputs / approved secret references
API -> Renderer: Workload + pinned templates + resolved bindings
Renderer -> Renderer: Bounded templates + semantic guards
Renderer --> API: Namespaced manifests
API -> Revision: Snapshot nonsecret bindings / manifest artifact + digest
API -> CD: Existing manifest delivery interface
CD --> API: Reconciliation / readiness
API --> Developer: Deployment result
@enduml
